  "text": "That’s where my page stops. I know what happened afterward, but I haven’t written that part. What would you like to hear?\n\nThank you for listening to it as it is. I’ll keep the page. There’s room at the bottom when I’m ready.\n\nI could bring the page as it is. If someone wants to know what happened next, I can start there.\n\nI’ll bring this version. I’d like to see what they think of the part after I packed my tools.\n\nAfter the last boat returns. I’ll keep my page ready. You won’t have to come and fetch me.\n\nI might have another page to bring next time. It will probably have a repair in it.\n\nThat gives me something to add when I work on the ending. Thank you for listening.\n\nLater, she came to my workshop with a loaf of bread. She brought it to thank me.\n\nI’ll bring your suggested ending. We can show the part of my story you chose.\n\nThe usual time, then. I’ll bring the page. Thank you for making room for it.\n\nThat’s as far as I’ve written. What would you like to hear about next?\n\nYes. The flour stayed dry, and Rina baked the bread she promised.\n\nLater, Rina came to my workshop with a loaf of bread to thank me.\n\nI didn't think anyone would want to hear about fixing a roof.\n\nFor me? I only replaced one tile. You’ve done all the baking.\n\nYes. The flour stayed dry, and she baked the bread that day.\n\nI’ll bring your suggested ending and the picture you chose.\n\nI'll add this part to the page and share it with everyone.\n\n“Unless you want us to eat standing like this.”\n\n“We’ll need to secure the corners,”\n\n“Bring the same cake,”\n\nSol",
